course: dictionary
lesson: 7133
title: Penicillin: a word from science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary tells you what a word means, but a text often tells you more. Read the sentences around the word and look for clues. «In 1928 Alexander Fleming noticed that a mould on a dish had killed the bacteria around it, which led to penicillin, a medicine that has saved many millions of lives.» The comma after penicillin is a clue: the words after it explain what penicillin is.
explain: The sentence says penicillin is a medicine, and that it came from a mould that killed bacteria. So you can work out that penicillin is a medicine made from a mould. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «a medicine made from a mould that kills many bacteria» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Some clues are about what a word does, not what it looks like. «Penicillin is an antibiotic used to treat infections.» An infection is a sickness caused by germs, and an antibiotic is a medicine that fights them. If a word is used to treat something, it helps to make that thing better.
fact: Penicillin is a medicine made from a mould that kills many bacteria.
fact: Penicillin is an antibiotic, which means it is used to treat infections.
fact: «Penicillin» is an uncountable noun, so we say «a course of penicillin», not «two penicillins».
fact: Alexander Fleming noticed in 1928 that a mould had killed bacteria on a dish, and this led to penicillin.
fact: Some people are allergic to penicillin, so doctors need to know before they give it to someone.
exercise: «The mould killed the bacteria around it on the dish.» What does killed tell you about the bacteria? | They grew bigger | They moved to a new dish | *They died | They turned into mould
exercise: «Penicillin is a medicine made from a mould that kills many bacteria.» What is penicillin? | A holiday Fleming took in 1928 | A type of bacteria that makes people ill | *A medicine made from a mould | A kind of dish used in a science lab
exercise: «a mould called Penicillium had killed the bacteria around it on a dish.» Find and copy the name of the mould. | *Penicillium | bacteria | Fleming | dish
test: «Eating mouldy food is not a medicine and can make you ill.» Why is mouldy bread not the same as penicillin? | Because mouldy bread is a kind of medicine too | Because both are sold in shops | *Because penicillin is a medicine made carefully from a mould, and mouldy food is not | Because penicillin is bread that has gone bad
test: «Some people are allergic to penicillin, so doctors ask about it first.» What does this tell you? | Penicillin tastes sweet | Penicillin is only for animals | *Some people's bodies react badly to penicillin | Everyone should take penicillin every day
exam: «Alexander Fleming discovered penicillin, the first widely used antibiotic, in 1928.» Which answer best explains what penicillin is? | A holiday in 1928 | A kind of mould that makes people ill | *A medicine that fights bacteria and infections | A dish that grows mould
